@*
    Shared store logo / fallback-icon partial.

    Used anywhere a store's logo needs to render with a graceful fallback
    (an icon in a colored circle) when no LogoURL is set. Previously this
    exact if/else block was duplicated in three places on the Store Owner
    Home page (profile header, side panel, post header) — this partial
    collapses the two truly-identical ones (profile header + side panel)
    into one place. The post header uses a different fallback pattern
    (a static placeholder image instead of an icon) so it was left as-is.

    Expected model (anonymous object or dynamic), e.g.:

    <partial name="/Pages/StoreOwner/Shared/_StoreLogoOrFallback"
             model="new {
                 LogoUrl = Model.Store?.LogoURL,
                 AltText = Model.Store?.StoreName,
                 ImgClass = "profile-avatar",
                 FallbackClass = "profile-avatar-fallback",
                 IconClass = "fa-store"
             }" />
*@
@model dynamic
@{
    string? logoUrl = Model.LogoUrl;
    string altText = Model.AltText ?? "Store";
    string imgClass = Model.ImgClass;
    string fallbackClass = Model.FallbackClass;
    string iconClass = Model.IconClass ?? "fa-store";
}
@if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(logoUrl))
{
    <img class="@imgClass" src="@logoUrl" alt="@altText Logo" />
}
else
{
    <div class="@fallbackClass">
        <i class="fas @iconClass"></i>
    </div>
}
